# THE 19-POINT LAUNCH & COMPLIANCE CHECKLIST

### Group A: Security & Infrastructure (Critical Priority)
5. **Secrets off the frontend:** Scan `src/`, `index.html`, and `vite.config.*` for hardcoded API keys, Bhashini credentials, Google Speech API keys, or `VITE_` prefixed secrets that should be proxied via a secure backend/edge function. Verify `.env` is in `.gitignore`.
7. **Force HTTPS:** Check hosting config (`vercel.json`, `netlify.toml`, `.htaccess`, or Firebase/Hostinger headers) for HTTP-to-HTTPS 301 redirects and Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS) headers.
18. **Spam protection:** Check all public forms (feedback, contact, recitation request, waitlist) for rate-limiting, honeypot fields, or CAPTCHA/Turnstile integration.

### Group B: Legal & Privacy Compliance
2. **Privacy policy page:** Verify a dedicated `/privacy-policy` route/page exists, explicitly detailing how user text inputs are processed via Bhashini and Google Speech APIs, data retention policies, and user rights.
3. **Terms & conditions page:** Verify a dedicated `/terms` route/page exists covering acceptable use for TTS generation, intellectual property/audio rights, and service disclaimers.
4. **Cookie consent banner:** Check for a non-intrusive, GDPR/DPDP-compliant cookie consent banner that blocks non-essential analytics scripts until explicit user opt-in.

### Group C: Technical SEO & Indexing
1. **Sitemap + robots.txt:** Verify `public/robots.txt` exists (allowing crawlers and pointing to the sitemap) and `public/sitemap.xml` (or automated Vite build plugin) dynamically includes all public routes (`/`, `/privacy-policy`, `/terms`, etc.).
6. **Social preview image:** Check `index.html` for Open Graph (`og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image`, `og:url`) and Twitter Card (`twitter:card`, `twitter:image`) meta tags pointing to a valid `1200x630px` preview banner.
9. **Meta titles & descriptions:** Verify dynamic or route-specific `<title>` (50–60 chars) and `<meta name="description">` (150–160 chars) tags across all views (e.g., using `react-helmet-async` or native document head management).
10. **Custom 404 page:** Verify the router has a wildcard catch-all (`path="*"`) rendering a branded, helpful 404 page with navigation back to the TTS studio—not a blank screen or host default.
15. **Favicon:** Check `index.html` and `public/` for complete favicon support (`favicon.ico`, `favicon.svg`, `apple-touch-icon.png`, and `site.webmanifest`).
16. **Fix broken links:** Audit all internal `<Link>`/`<a>` routes, footer links, audio asset URLs, and external documentation/API links for 404s or dead anchors.

### Group D: UX, Accessibility & Frontend Quality
8. **Mobile responsiveness:** Audit Tailwind CSS breakpoints (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`) across the TTS input box, language selectors, audio player controls, and navigation drawers to ensure zero horizontal overflow on 360px–414px viewports.
11. **Alt text for images:** Scan all `<img>` and `<svg>` elements for descriptive `alt` attributes (or `aria-hidden="true"` for purely decorative icons).
14. **Color contrast ratio:** Check Tailwind color combinations (text vs. background, disabled buttons, audio waveform/progress indicators) against WCAG AA standards (minimum 4.5:1 for normal text).
17. **Form validation:** Check TTS text input fields (character limits, unsupported script/character warnings, empty state handling) and contact/feedback forms for real-time client-side validation and accessible error messages.

### Group E: Performance & Telemetry
12. **Image compression:** Audit `public/` and `src/assets/` for uncompressed PNG/JPG files; flag any assets over 150KB for WebP/AVIF conversion.
13. **Check page load speed:** Audit bundle size, lazy loading (`React.lazy` / `Suspense` for secondary pages like Privacy/Terms), font loading (`font-display: swap`), and unused dependencies in `package.json`.
19. **Set-up analytics:** Check `index.html` or analytics utility modules for privacy-friendly analytics (e.g., GA4 with IP anonymization or Plausible/Umami) gated behind the Cookie Consent state, plus custom events for TTS generation triggers.

