Key SutraSparsh-Specific Risks to Watch During the Audit
1. API Key Exposure (#5): Because SutraSparsh integrates Bhashini and Google Speech APIs, make sure your audit strictly flags any VITE_BHASHINI_API_KEY or VITE_GOOGLE_SPEECH_KEY variables. Anything prefixed with VITE_ is compiled directly into your public JavaScript bundle. If those keys are currently in the frontend, move the TTS API calls to a lightweight serverless proxy (e.g., Cloudflare Worker, Vercel Edge Function, or Firebase Cloud Function) before launch.
2. DPDP Act & Speech Data Disclosure (#2 & #4): Since SutraSparsh processes Indian regional languages and operates out of India, your Privacy Policy should explicitly state whether user-entered text and synthesized audio are processed transiently in memory or logged by third-party APIs (Bhashini/Google).
3. SPA Routing vs. Crawlers (#1 & #10): In a Vite/React SPA, search engines sometimes struggle to index client-side routes unless robots.txt, sitemap.xml, and server-side fallback rewrites (routing all traffic to index.html while serving a proper 404 UI for unknown paths) are configured together.
